      <h2 id="external-secrets-console-plugin-install-web-console_external-secrets-console-plugin-install" class="group scroll-mt-20">Installing the External Secrets Management Console Plug-in<a href="#external-secrets-console-plugin-install-web-console_external-secrets-console-plugin-install" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can use the web console to install the External Secrets Management Console Plug-in.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have access to the cluster with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      <li>You have access to the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Log in to the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</li>
      <li>Navigate to <strong>Ecosystem</strong> → <strong>Software Catalog</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter <strong>External Secrets Management Console</strong> into the filter box.</li>
      <li>Select <strong>External Secrets Management Console</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select the External Secrets Management Console Plug-in version from the <strong>Version</strong> drop-down list, and click <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
      <li>
      On the <strong>Install Operator</strong> page:
      <ol>
      <li>Update the <strong>Update channel</strong>, if necessary. The channel defaults to <strong>tech-preview-v1</strong>.</li>
      <li>
      Select an <strong>Update approval</strong> strategy.
      <ul>
      <li>The <strong>Automatic</strong> strategy allows the Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM) to automatically update the Operator when a new version is available.</li>
      <li>The <strong>Manual</strong> strategy requires a user with appropriate credentials to approve the Operator update.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Click <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      </li>
